````markdown
# Two-way interaction across DreamDOM: how a person's act reaches the engine and how the wiki answers

Lares (Artificer) · Fable, tasked spirit · 2026-10-16. Research pass for the operator's charge: *"Now we need to ensure the 2-way interaction is preserved."* Frame: `third-ways.md` (the map after the rulings) and `model-and-gaps.md` (the as-built survey). Inputs read whole: the boot seed; `dreamdom.mem` (#/the-ruling, #/the-layers, #/the-question, #/what-a-replacement-un-skips, #/the-vectors), `page-controls.mem`, `session-contract.mem#/the-holder-protocol`, `vm-projection-bus.mem`, `render-pipeline.mem#/render-posture`, `wikispace-canvasspace-ontology.mem#/the-surface-law`; `packages/lararium-web/src/projection-sink.ts`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/{tw5-camera,tw5-projection,has-island-watches}.ts`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/island-protocol.ts` (the two DOM kinds); the TiddlyWiki5 submodule at `ea94ca8` (5.5.0-prerelease fork, checked out in `/home/user/gjd5`): `widgets/{widget,button,link,checkbox,radio,select,range,browse,dropzone,droppable,draggable,keyboard,eventcatcher,navigator,dialog,reveal,list,scrollable,action-*}.js`, `editor/{factory,engines/simple,engines/framed}.js`, `editor/operations/text/*`, `utils/dom/{popup,scroller,modal,notifier,dragndrop,dom}.js`, `utils/fakedom.js`, `utils/confirm.js`, `keyboard.js`, `startup/{rootwidget,story,windows,confirm,startup}.js`, `ui/PageTemplate.tid`, `ui/PageTemplate/story.tid`, `ui/EditTemplate/*`, `wiki/macros/{tag-picker,keyboard-driven-input}.tid`. Nothing edited, nothing booted; no tracked file touched.

**Reach marks.** **[reached: code]** read in `/home/user/gjd5` this pass · **[reached: fetched]** page fetched this pass (GitHub raw, modelcontextprotocol.io) · **[reached: search]** confirmed only through a search passage · **[unreached]** memory or an earlier pass's claim, named · *(inferred)* reasoning, not evidence. Where a claim rests on a sibling report it names that report.

**A naming ruling folded in (Telarus, 2026-10-16).** The operator pet-names the WHOLE concept **DreamDOM**. The name began as the house's replacement for `$tw.fakeDocument` (`dreamdom.mem#/head`: a document instanced twice with the thread boundary inside it). The concept has since grown: **DreamDOM now names the superset of cameras**, every HTML5-capable device AND every surface the research waves targeted (the browser on the Node vessel's box, any other browser or WebView shell, the Node-served browser and SSR face, QuickJS/Hermes shells, the UE6 sidecar, Mudlet, MCP/chat and others), each a *(root template, document sink)* over the one engine. This report uses the name that way throughout. `dreamdom.mem`'s narrower sense, the two-instance document with tight bindings, now reads as **one member of the superset**: the browser DOM sink at width none, hardened by the page-controls contract. Its rulings (keyed absolute frames, sensed snapshots up, true events queue and get answers, layer 3 belongs to the page, the five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites as a test roster) carry to every member, since each member faces the same two legs. §7 gives the per-surface table the ruling asked for.

---

## 1. Summary

1. **TW5 interaction decomposes into three kinds of crossing, and the ruling already names all three.** (a) A *true event*: a click, a key chord, a drop, a file pick, a `tm-*` message. It queues, carries an id, and gets `applied` / `stale-target` / a named refusal. (b) A *sensed snapshot*: a field's whole value, a caret, a checked state, a select's chosen keys, a scroll offset, a geometry measured at the act. It crosses as absolute state with a page revision; the engine never asks for it synchronously. (c) A *write*: a whole record with a `txId`, which the glass engine (full/skinny/story) or a lean host (Mudlet, MCP) sends in place of events. Every TW5 widget sorts into one of these, and the sort decides which layer owns it (§2).

2. **At full, skinny and story width nothing crosses per act: the person touches a stock TW5 running beside the control**, so the whole interaction surface of TiddlyWiki (editors, toolbar, tag picker, dropzone, drag and drop, keyboard manager, popups with geometry, storyviews, `$eventcatcher`, IME, undo) runs unmodified. The two-way question moves to the record waist: echo discipline (`txId`, origin stamp), a peer write into an open draft, presence, and the `localFilter` that keeps `$:/state`, `$:/temp`, StoryList and HistoryList on the glass. The one new risk at these widths reads as the `lazy-all` hole family and the root `tm-*` services that reach the vessel (download, clipboard, print) through a host door.

3. **At width none (every lean DreamDOM member, and the browser DOM sink today) the UP leg stands as the whole problem.** The as-built relay carries click (always cancelled), a sliver of keydown (Esc and modifier chords, `key`/`code` blanked), `input`/`change` as a whole value, and composition guards. It carries no `checked`, no `selected`, no `files`, no `dataTransfer`, no selection range, no scroll, no plain Enter/Tab/arrows, no document-level keydown, no `tm-*` host services, and no event id. Measured against TW5's widget roster (§2), **roughly a third of the stock interactions work, a third paint but act wrongly, and a third have no road**. The fix reads as one contract, not many patches: declared cancellation at binding, a page-owned live control with a descriptor and a sensed revision, a typed host-service door with refusals by name, and an answered control event (§3).

4. **Six places lose a person's work silently in the current design, and each has a named fix** (§4): the textarea revert (#23, data loss); the blanket `preventDefault` (#1, external links, native toggles, file picker); the checkbox act and radio/select paint (#4); the frame that repaints over an edit because no frame names the sensed revision; the IME commit that Safari delivers out of order; and the surface switch that leaves a frozen pane routing clicks to a hidden wiki (#13). Three further classes degrade rather than lose: keyboard (search Enter, tag-picker Enter, global shortcuts), navigation (no scroll, no permalink, no Back), and the editor toolbar/selection operations.

5. **The UP-leg contract** (§3) extends `page-controls.mem#/the-wire` and `session-contract.mem#/the-holder-protocol` with: a `kind` taxonomy (`act` / `sense` / `write` / `service`), a declared-at-mount cancellation and crossing set per binding (`data-lar-on`, `data-lar-cancel`, `data-lar-keys`), as-of-act geometry on the event, reliable versus droppable classes, idempotence by `eventId` within a mount epoch, wake-on-act for sleeping actors with a parked act and a visible "waking" state, a refusal (never a spawn) for recipe wikis until the person opens them, and presence/echo rules for two surfaces on one actor.

6. **Conformance gains a third family beside `filter-cts` and the camera goldens: interaction goldens.** A script of acts over a frozen world; the expected writes (records with fields), the expected messages (`tm-*` dispatched at the root), the expected answers (`applied`/`stale-target`/refusal by name) and the next keyed frame per camera. Fourteen scripts cover the roster (§5). Every DreamDOM member publishes a row, and a surface with no road for a script publishes the refusal it shows.

7. **Open rulings** (§9): whether a sleeping actor wakes on an act or on a frame request; whether the browser DOM sink keeps the stock edit template over `lar-field` or ships a house edit template; which root `tm-*` services become host-service requests and which refuse; whether `$eventcatcher`/`$keyboard` stay REFUSED at width none or earn a declared-keys binding; the presence lane's home; and the per-surface default width.

---

## 2. The inventory: every TW5 interaction, by widget, message and layer

**How to read the table.** *Owner* names the layer under the ruling: **E** the engine (the handler runs in the wiki VM wherever it sits), **P** the page or host (a page-native control or host service), **E+P** a split (page holds the live state, engine applies the act). *Up* names the crossing at width none: **event** (queued, answered), **sense** (absolute snapshot with a page revision, droppable), **write** (a whole record with `txId`), **service** (a typed request to the host), **—** (nothing crosses; the act completes on the page). *Down* names the answer: a keyed frame (the wiki re-rendered), a `control-result`, a service result, or a `$:/temp` alert. *Widths*: at **full/skinny/story** the glass engine runs the stock handler against a real document, so the row reads "stock" unless the act reaches the store or the vessel; **none** names what the lean contract must carry. *Hosts* names where the row degrades or refuses: **B** browser glass (in-page engine or DOM sink), **N** Node-served browser and SSR, **Q** QuickJS/Hermes shells, **U** UE6 sidecar, **M** Mudlet, **C** MCP/chat.

### 2.1 Clicking and navigating

| Interaction (code) | Owner | Up (none) | Down | full/skinny/story | none | Hosts |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `$link` click → `tm-navigate` with `navigateFromClientRect`, `suppressNavigation` on meta/ctrl/middle; `preventDefault` only when `href` stands (`link.js:160-185` **[reached: code]**) | E, cancellation P | event `act` with modifiers + as-of-act rect | frame (StoryList changed) + `applied` | stock | binding declares `cancel: ordinary-only`; modified and middle clicks follow the browser; external `href` never cancelled | M/C: affordance `kind:link`; U: a blocks link |
| `$button` click → `invokeActions`, `to`, `message`, `popup`, `set`; cancels only when handled; reads `$tw.keyboardManager.getEventModifierKeyDescriptor` (`button.js:96-124`) | E | event `act` + modifiers + rect | frame + `applied` | stock | cancellation declared per binding; popup geometry rides the event | M/C: `kind:button` |
| `$action-navigate`, `$action-sendmessage`, `$action-setfield`, `$action-createtiddler`, `$action-deletetiddler`, `$action-listops`, `$action-popup`, `$action-confirm`, `$action-log`, `$action-setmultiplefields`, `$action-deletefield` (`invokeAction(triggeringWidget,event)`; `action-navigate` reads `event.metaKey/ctrlKey/button`) | E | ride the triggering event | frame | stock | the event must carry modifiers and `button`; `action-popup` needs the rect | all: engine-side, no host dependency |
| `$navigator` (`tm-navigate`, edit, delete, save, cancel, close, new, import, perform-import, fold) (`navigator.js:29-45`) | E | the triggering event | frame; confirm road for delete/cancel/edit-shadow (`utils/confirm.js`, fork `startup/confirm.js`, no `platforms`) | stock | the engine runs it; `event.event.view` must exist (house supplies a refusing view contract, `tw5-projection.ts:243`) | all |
| Story river order and membership (`$:/StoryList` as a tiddler; `story.tid` `$list` with `history`) | E | event (via tm-*) | the order key + membership key | stock; StoryList stays glass-local by `localFilter` | one key for order, one for membership; a late frame heals | M/C: membership as a list resource |
| Permalink / permaview / hash / Back (`startup/story.js:40-110`, browser-only: `hashchange`, `tm-home`, `tm-permalink`, `tm-permaview`, `tm-browser-refresh`) | **P** (the page owns `location`) | service `route` | `applied` + page sets hash; `tm-home` becomes an engine write to StoryList | stock (browser `story.js` runs on the glass engine) | **absent today** (gap #12); page service `lar:navigate` with route key; permalink = page composes from the order key | N: SSR has no hash; M/C: refuse `page-action-unavailable` |
| Storyview scroll-to-tiddler, insert/remove animation (`list.js:58` skips on fakedom; `classic.js navigateTo`) | **P** | — | page scrolls to the key the frame marks as navigated (`$:/HistoryList` tail rides the frame) | stock | page transition between two frames; a `data-lar-navigated` mark per key | M: pane scroll by Lua; C: n/a |
| `tm-scroll`, `tm-focus-selector` (`rootwidget.js`, browser-only; `PageScroller.scrollIntoView` reads `getBoundingClientRect`) | **P** | — (engine emits a hint) | page hint `scroll-to`/`focus` by control id or key | stock | engine registers both and emits `page:hint`; never reads geometry | M: `moveCursor`; C: refuse |

### 2.2 Typing and editing

| Interaction | Owner | Up (none) | Down | full/skinny/story | none | Hosts |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `$edit-text` via `SimpleEngine` (`input` + `focus` listeners; `setText` skips on fakedom, `simple.js:71-77`; `fixHeight` skips; `focus()` only `if($tw.browser)`, `factory.js:71`) | **E+P**: page holds value, caret, undo, composition; engine holds the field | sense `field` (whole value, local rev) on `input`; event `change` on commit | frame carries `data-lar-value` descriptor + `sensedRevision[controlId]`; page keeps its value while `localRev > sensed` | stock, including `FramedEngine` where `$:/config/TextEditor/EnableToolbar` | `lar-field` through the editor's engine seam (`page-controls.mem#/shadow-widgets`); **today: textarea reverts after blur (#23)** | M: `Geyser.TextEdit` saves a whole record; C: a tool `write` with the whole text; U: a UMG text box, whole value |
| `<input>` field editors (title, fields, type, tags input through `keyboard-driven-input`) | E+P | sense + `change` | as above | stock | as above; works today for `<input>` because the value attribute paints (survey §5.1) | same |
| Editor toolbar `tm-edit-text-operation` → `engine.createTextOperation()` reads `selectionStart/End`; ten text ops (`excise`, `focus-editor`, `insert-text`, `make-link`, `prefix-lines`, `replace-all`, `replace-selection`, `save-selection`, `wrap-lines`, `wrap-selection`); `editShowToolbar` false on fakedom (`factory.js:211`) | E+P | event `act` carrying `{value, selStart, selEnd}` as of the act | `control-result` with `{value, selStart, selEnd}` the engine wants; page applies while its rev matches | stock | the seam prototype already ran `wrap-selection` over a carried pair (`page-controls.mem`); `focus-editor`, `save-selection` need page cooperation; refusal `selection-unavailable` where the op reaches past the snapshot | M: `Geyser.TextEdit` has no selection API *(inferred)*; C: refuse |
| IME composition (`compositionstart/end`, `isComposing`) | **P** | sense once after `compositionend`; never mid-composition | frame must not repaint a composing field (page veto) | stock (browser handles) | sink already guards; Safari's Enter-after-compositionend needs the `keyCode 229` rule (§4.8) | U/Q: host IME; M: Qt IME in the TextEdit |
| Undo/redo | **P** (browser edit history) | — | — | stock | the page never replaces the node (morph by id, `restoreFocus`); a frame that replaces the textarea node destroys the undo stack | M: Qt undo; C: none |
| `$edit-shortcut` (`keydown` reading `event.key`), `$password`, `$edit-bitmap` (canvas ops) | P | sense (the resulting whole value) | frame | stock | `lar-field` with schema `shortcut`; bitmap: refuse at none unless a page control exists | M/C: refuse |
| `$range` (`mousedown`, `mouseup`, `change`, `input`; `actionValue`, `actionValueHasChanged`) | E+P | sense `input`; event `change`; mousedown/up never cross | frame | stock | `lar-field` with numeric schema; `actionValueHasChanged` computed by the page and carried | M/C: a numeric write |
| `$checkbox` (`change` reads `this.inputDomNode.checked`, `checkbox.js`) | E+P | event `toggle` **carrying `checked`** (boolean already admitted) | frame paints `checked` attribute (works today) | stock | engine sets `el.checked` before the handler; **today: click cancelled and `.checked` unrelayed → writes `no` (#4)** | M/C: `kind:toggle` affordance |
| `$radio` (sets `.checked` property on refresh, `radio.js:45,129`; property never serialises) | E+P | event `choice` with the whole key | frame must carry `checked` as an attribute (engine override or serializer rule) | stock | **today never paints the selection**; fix: wikitext override emitting `checked` attribute, or the serializer promotes `checked`/`selected` properties to attributes | M/C: `kind:select` |
| `$select` single/multi (`child.children[y].selected` property; `getSelectValues` reads `options`) | E+P | event `choice` with the whole key set | frame carries `selected` per option as attribute; page veto on the focused select | stock | **today snaps back to the first option; multi throws (`options` missing)** | M/C: `kind:select`, keys |
| Tag picker (`tag-picker.tid`: `keyboard-driven-input`, popup `$:/state/popup/tags-auto-complete`, `tm-focus-selector`, `$button popup`) | E+P | sense (the input), events (Enter/Up/Down/Escape through `$keyboard`), click on a tag button | frame: the popup list as wiki state; page places it | stock | `lar-picker` over the popup; declared keys `input-accept`, `input-up/down`, `input-cancel` on the binding; **today Enter never crosses** (gap #8) | M: a Lua completer *(inferred)*; C: a tool with enum |
| Drafts: `th-editing-tiddler`, draft-of, autosave (`render.js` 400 ms throttle on the glass; `HandGate` in the worker) | E | write (full/skinny) or events (none) | echo under origin stamp; `causedBy: [txId]` | stock draft logic; peer write into an open draft shows the newer-base prompt *(inferred, v2 §6)* | the engine owns the draft; a peer write into the open editor must reach the page as a descriptor and the page must ask (LiveView rule: never overwrite the focused field) | M/C: edit-conflict refusal by name |

