### 2.6 Root `tm-*` host services (the rootwidget family, every one browser-only upstream)

| Message (source) | Owner | Up (none) | Down | full/skinny/story | none | Hosts |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `tm-copy-to-clipboard` (`dom.js:237`, `execCommand("copy")`) | **P** | service `clipboard` (user-activation bound) | service result → `tm-notify` success/failure | stock on the glass engine | engine registers the handler and posts `glass:service{kind:"clipboard", text}`; absent today | M: `setClipboardText` *(memory)*; C: the text in the reply; N (SSR): refuse |
| `tm-download-file` (`saver-handler.js:103`) | P | service `download{filename, type, text}` | `applied` | stock | as above | M: write a file; C: a resource; U: refuse |
| `tm-print`, `tm-full-screen`, `tm-open-window`, `tm-close-window`, `tm-close-all-windows`, `tm-open-external-window`, `tm-browser-refresh` | P | service, allowlisted; `tm-open-window` opens a *second camera* (the windows startup mounts a second root over `srcDocument`) | `applied` or `page-action-unavailable` | stock | refuse by name today; `tm-open-window` becomes "open a second surface on this actor" (§3.6) | M/C/U: refuse by name |
| `tm-http-request`, `tm-http-cancel-all-requests` (`$tw.httpClient`) | **E, gated** (an authority question under Web3-only law) | — | the binding tiddlers the request names | runs on the glass engine today, ungated | refused by default; a capability-gated host fetch behind the causal-island boundary if ever allowed | all: refuse unless the manifest grants `http` |
| `tm-rename-tiddler`, `tm-relink-tiddler`, `tm-home` | E | the triggering event | frame | stock | pure wiki logic; land worker-side in an island startup module (survey §5.3) | all |
| `tm-save-wiki`, `tm-auto-save-wiki` (saver-handler), `tm-login/logout/server-refresh` (syncer) | **n/a** | — | — | no saver, no syncer (rejected) | refuse by name; the store saves itself | all |
| `tm-confirm` (fork `startup/confirm.js`, no `platforms`) | E | the answer click | frame | runs everywhere | runs today | all |
| `tm-verse-event` (`vm-projection-bus.mem`) | E → vessel | — | verb result | works | works | all |

**Reading the roster.** Of fifty-odd `tm-*` kinds the core dispatches (`grep` over `core/modules` **[reached: code]**), the navigator's fifteen, the fieldmangler's four, `tm-confirm`, `tm-edit-text-operation` and `tm-verse-event` run in the engine wherever it sits. Nine (`rootwidget.js`) plus seven (`story.js`) plus three (`windows.js`) plus one (`saver-handler.js`) bind only under `platforms: ["browser"]`, and the third runtime skips them all. Half of those read as pure wiki logic the island can register itself; the other half name a host service, and each DreamDOM member says which it carries (§7).

---

## 3. The UP-leg contract

This section extends `page-controls.mem#/the-wire` (one keyed frame down, one answered event up) and `session-contract.mem#/the-holder-protocol` (`wiki:control-event` → `projection:control-result`; `schemaVersion`, `ownerEpoch`, `sessionId`, `generation`, `surfaceId`, `mountEpoch` on every message). Nothing here reopens the rulings; it fills the fields the roster in §2 showed missing.

### 3.1 Four kinds on one leg

```
wiki:control-event {
  eventId, sessionId, surfaceId, cameraId, mountEpoch,
  kind: "act" | "sense" | "write" | "service-result",
  controlId | renderId | affordanceId,     // one of; renderId retires into controlId as bindings get names
  controlType,                             // link | button | toggle | choice | field | key | key-global |
                                           // drop | import-offer | order | scroll | drag-start | drag-end | confirm
  action,                                  // the binding's declared act name
  seenFrameRev,                            // the key revision the page had painted when the person acted
  seenMembershipRev,
  localRev?,                               // the page's own revision of a sensed control
  wholeValue?,                             // whole string | whole key set | whole ordered id list | bounded bytes
  modifiers?: {meta, ctrl, alt, shift, button, repeat},
  key?: {key, code, keyCode, isComposing},
  geometry?: {rect, scroll}                // as-of-act, answers THIS event's handler only (dreamdom ruling 4)
}
projection:control-result { eventId, controlId, status: "applied" | "stale-target" | "refused", reason?, want?: {value, selStart, selEnd} }
```

- **`act`** queues, carries an id, and gets exactly one answer (ruling condition 5). It names a binding the frame declared.
- **`sense`** carries absolute page state with `localRev`; it never queues behind acts, it coalesces newest-wins, and it never gets a per-message answer: its answer reads as `sensedRevision[controlId]` in a later frame (ruling condition 4). A `sense` with an `eventId` becomes an `act` (a `change` commit).
- **`write`** carries a whole record with `txId` and `basis` (v2 P14): the glass engine's leg at full/skinny/story, and a lean host's edit leg (Mudlet's `Lar.Write`, an MCP `write` tool). It answers `port:written` and echoes `causedBy:[txId]`. **Writes travel as writes, never as events** (the ruling), so an edit at width none ends as a `write` from the page-native control the moment the control commits, never as a replayed keystroke.
- **`service-result`** closes a `glass:service` request the engine made (clipboard, download, route) with `ok` or a named refusal, so `tm-copy-to-clipboard` can fire its own success notification through the engine.

### 3.2 Declared at mount, never decided at handling

The frame carries the declarations beside each key, the way WorkerDOM put the flag in its subscribe opcode and coincident declares `invoke: "preventDefault"` at binding (`model-and-gaps.md` §5.2; WorkerDOM's compat table still marks `preventDefault()`, `stopPropagation()`, `dispatchEvent()`, `focus()` on non-inputs, `activeElement`, every `Selection.*` and `Range.*` row, `selectionStart/End`, `setSelectionRange`, `getBoundingClientRect()` and `checked` unsupported **[reached: fetched]**; Blazor reached the same shape as the `@onclick:preventDefault` attribute because its handler runs after SignalR **[reached: search]**; remote-dom declares `remoteEvents` statically on the element class and events do not bubble unless the remote side asks **[reached: fetched]**).

| Stamp | Set by | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `data-lar-on="click keydown change"` | the patched `addEventListener` | the types this node binds; the page relays only these |
| `data-lar-cancel="click:ordinary"` / `"keydown:declared"` / `"dragover"` | the widget class, through a small table (link: ordinary clicks with `href`; button: when handled, which the page cannot know, so `always` for `$button` with `actions|to|message|popup|set`; keyboard: declared keys; dropzone/droppable: dragenter/dragover/drop) | what the page cancels synchronously |
| `data-lar-keys="enter escape alt-shift-N"` | `$keyboard` and `$edit-text` through `parseKeyDescriptors` | the crossing set; other keys never leave the page |
| `data-lar-bubble="keydown"` | the engine | which types the engine bubbles up its fake tree (today only keydown; §4.2 asks for click to bubble to the first listener and answer `unclaimed`) |
| `data-lar-live` + `data-lar-value` / `data-lar-checked` / `data-lar-selected` | the engine, per refresh | the descriptor the page reconciles its live control against |
| `data-lar-drag-titles` *(proposed)* | `makeDraggable` sites at render | the `text/vnd.tiddler` payload the page sets on `dragstart` |
| membership key `shortcuts` *(proposed)* | the engine from `$:/tags/KeyboardShortcut` | the global descriptor set the page listens for on its document |

A node whose `data-lar-on` lacks the event type never relays, and the browser default stands: external links open, native toggles toggle, the file picker opens.

### 3.3 Ordering, idempotence, classes

- **One FIFO per surface for `act`s**, in the order the person made them; the engine applies them in arrival order and answers each. The page may pipeline (send the next before the answer) because every act names `seenFrameRev`; an act whose target key has moved past `seenFrameRev` with a *different binding at that control id* answers `stale-target`; one whose binding still stands applies (Discord's `custom_id` survives message edits the same way **[reached: search]**).
- **Idempotence by `eventId` within a `mountEpoch`.** A resend after a lost answer carries the same id; the engine keeps a small answer ring per surface and re-answers without re-applying. The ring dies with the mount.
- **Reliable class** (`act`, `write`, `service-result`): never dropped, retried until answered or the surface closes. **Droppable class** (`sense`, presence): newest wins, no retry, no answer.
- **Frames never answer events.** A frame says what it sensed (`sensedRevision`); the answer travels on `control-result`. Today's `stale-target` painted into the next frame as an `<output>` (`tw5-projection.ts:330`) reaches no frame when the surface switched; the id-correlated answer fixes that (`page-controls.mem#/the-sink-today`, fault 3).
- **Geometry rides the act, never a reply.** The link's rect, the popup anchor, the drop position answer that event's handler and no other (today's `_larRect` on the fake node persists past the event *(inferred from `tw5-projection.ts:222-227`)*; the contract scopes it to the dispatch).
- **Netcode's shape, borrowed where it fits.** Inputs carry sequence numbers and the authority acks the last processed one; the client replays unacked inputs over fresh state **[reached: search]**. The house keeps the ids and the ack and drops the replay: both sides stay replicas (vector 4), and a page-native control already holds the person's truth, so nothing needs re-simulating.

### 3.4 Sleeping and recipe actors: what an act does

| Actor state | A person acts on its surface | Ruling proposed |
|---|---|---|
| **daemon / pinned** | normal | — |
| **sleeping** (store persisted, engine cold) | The surface still shows the last frames (the attachment keeps `{cursor, subscriptions, width, actorKey, cameraMount}`). The act **parks** on the holder with its `eventId`, the surface shows a `waking` state beside the control (not a spinner over the page), the actor wakes, replays the attachment, re-renders, and answers the parked act against the woken frame: `applied` if the binding still stands, `stale-target` with a fresh frame if not. A `sense` during sleep stays on the page and lands as the first `sensedRevision` after wake. | **Wake on act, yes**, bounded: one parked act per surface; a second act while waking replaces the first and the first answers `superseded` *(new status, open ruling 9.1)*. |
| **recipe** (a bag stack, no actor) | No surface exists, so no act exists; the only act reads as *open*, which spawns. A link from another wiki into a recipe wiki (`lar:` cross-wiki navigate) answers `refused: actor-not-spawned` with an affordance `spawn`. | **Never spawn on an incidental act**; spawn only on an explicit open. |
| **hibernating mid-edit** | `page-controls` keeps the field's value on the page; the holder refuses to hibernate an actor with an unanswered reliable act; a `sense` never blocks hibernation. | the liveness budget frees resources, never drops a reliable act (`session-contract#/how-a-session-ends`). |

### 3.5 Multi-tab and multi-device: two surfaces on one actor

- **Two tabs, one actor, width none.** Each tab opens its own surface under its own session (`session-contract#/the-browser`); the actor mounts one camera per surface (the keyed-frame camera already holds per-mount `roots`, `renderIds`, `liveIds` in `ProjectionEventScope`). `$:/state`, popups and the confirm question live in the engine today, so **two surfaces see one popup state**; the confirm road rules this as acceptable for one question ("two tabs over one shared island both see it and either may answer", `dreamdom.mem#/the-question`), and the port's tier filter (v2 P10) moves `$:/state` per surface at full/skinny/story. At none the engine must key `$:/state/*` per surface or accept shared popups; **open ruling 9.5**.
- **Two tabs at full/skinny.** Two replicas, one truth, one leader (v2 P15); each tab's own TW5 holds its own `$:/state`; presence tells each about the other's open draft (P13).
- **Two devices.** The CRDT merges; a peer write into an open editor reaches the page as a descriptor with a higher engine revision while the page's `localRev` exceeds the sensed one; the page keeps the person's text and shows "a newer version landed" beside the field with a *take theirs* affordance (the LiveView rule: the client stays the source of truth for a focused input; `phx-patch-focused` opts a field into patching **[reached: fetched]**; TW5's own draft logic shows the newer-base prompt at save on the glass engine).
- **Echo guard.** A `write` carries `txId`; the engine's `change` emits `causedBy:[txId]`; the originating adaptor drops it as foam (TW5-Yjs's origin-tagged transact, TidGi's titles-in-flight, v2 §0.3-0.5). At width none the page keeps a field's value while `localRev > sensedRevision`, which stands as the same guard at control grain.
- **Presence.** An ephemeral lane, never a tiddler (P13): `{surfaceId, actor, editing: [titles], focused: controlId}` with a 30 s expiry. At width none the engine can render presence into the frame as a key; at full/skinny the glass renders it from the lane.

### 3.6 Host services

`glass:service { requestId, kind: clipboard|download|route|open-surface|print|fullscreen|open-external, args, userActivation: true }` travels engine → surface; the surface answers `service-result`. A surface's manifest at `session:surface-open` lists the kinds it carries; a kind outside the list answers `page-action-unavailable` at once and the engine raises `$:/temp/lares/alert/refused/<kind>` (vector 5). `tm-open-window` reads as `open-surface{cameraRoot, tiddler}`: a second camera on the same actor, which `dreamdom.mem#/the-position` already treats as a composition.

---

## 4. Where interaction gets lost or degrades: the adversarial walk

Each row names the mechanism, the width where it bites, the fix, or the refusal by name. HIGH marks silent loss of a person's work; MED marks a visible failure; LOW marks a degradation with a workaround.

### 4.1 The five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites (`dreamdom.mem#/what-a-replacement-un-skips`)

| Site | What it skips | Width none today | Under the contract | full/skinny/story |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `editor/factory.js:211` (toolbar off) | the editor toolbar and its ten text operations | toolbar never renders | the seam engine renders the toolbar; each op carries `{value,sel}`; `focus-editor` and `save-selection` need page cooperation; ops that reach past the snapshot refuse `selection-unavailable` | stock, `FramedEngine` available |
| `simple.js:72` (`setText` guard) | the engine never pushes text into a fake node | **HIGH: textarea reverts after blur and the next keystroke overwrites earlier edits (#23)**; `updateDomNodeText` also no-ops because `value` lives in `attributes` while the textarea's child text paints | the frame carries `data-lar-value` and the page reconciles against it only while `localRev <= sensedRevision`; the seam engine's `setText` writes the descriptor, never the node | stock |
| `simple.js:105` / `framed.js:161` (`fixHeight`) | auto-height | fixed 400 px or `rows` | page sizes its own field (`field-sizing: content` where supported, else a measured resize) | stock |
| `list.js:58` (storyviews off) | scroll-to-navigated, insert/remove transitions | no scroll on navigate (#12) | page transition between frames; a `navigated` mark per key from `$:/HistoryList`'s tail | stock |
| `reveal.js:45,279` (popup positioning off) | `positionPopup` and `tc-popup` class | first-level popups placed from the click rect by the sink; nested popups, keyboard-opened popups and `$:/state` restored popups land unplaced *(inferred)* | `lar-popover` anchored by the page from the control's own box; the engine never positions | stock |

**The crucible rule stands**: these five un-skip together the first time a document presents as real. A DreamDOM member that keeps a fake document keeps them skipped **on purpose** and supplies the page half; a member that hosts the engine beside a real document (full/skinny/story, the Node-served browser with an in-page engine) un-skips all five and must walk them in a real browser before anything downstream gets believed.

### 4.2 The blanket `preventDefault` (#1) and the unbubbled click

`projection-sink.ts` cancels every click that resolves to a rid-bearing ancestor (the page template's `$dropzone` wrapper carries one, `PageTemplate.tid` **[reached: code]**), and the worker fires a click on its own node only (`tw5-projection.ts:254-262`: the loop breaks unless `keydown`). So a click on a plain checkbox inside the river cancels on the page and invokes nothing in the worker. **Loss:** external links, native toggles, the file picker, text selection by double-click in some engines, and the `<summary>` toggle. **Fix:** `data-lar-cancel` per binding (§3.2) and a worker that bubbles every type to the first listener and answers `unclaimed` so the page can leave the default alone. **Refusal:** none needed.

### 4.3 Checkbox, radio, select (#4 and the select snap-back)

Three different mechanisms, one descriptor fix. The checkbox act fails because the handler reads `.checked` the fake node never holds; the radio never paints because TW5 sets a *property* and fakedom serialises *attributes* only (`fakedom.js:139-146` keeps `attributes`, `value` as an attribute, no `checked`/`selected` property store **[reached: code]**); the select snaps back because Idiomorph re-syncs `option.selected` from the parsed HTML and the sink's focus guard covers only `input`/`textarea` (`projection-sink.ts:93-101` **[reached: code]**; Idiomorph offers `ignoreActive`, `ignoreActiveValue`, `restoreFocus` and the `beforeNodeMorphed`/`beforeAttributeUpdated` vetoes **[reached: fetched]**). **Fix:** the engine's serializer promotes `checked`/`selected` to attributes at flush, the event carries `checked` or the whole key set, the engine sets the fake property before invoking the handler, and `beforeNodeMorphed` returns `false` for a `data-lar-live` control whose `localRev` exceeds the frame's sensed revision. **Width:** none only; dissolves at full/skinny/story.

### 4.4 The frame that repaints over an edit

Without `sensedRevision` a frame rendered before a keystroke can land after it; today focus alone protects a field (`protectedValues` captured only for `shadow.activeElement` or composing fields). A field that lost focus a moment ago, a select, a checkbox, a `<details>` open state and a scroll offset all repaint from the older frame. **Fix:** condition 4 of the ruling, implemented per control: `sensedRevision[controlId]` in the frame, `localRev` on the sense, page veto while `localRev > sensed`. **Width:** none; at full/skinny the glass TW5 owns the node and TW5's own `setText` guard (`activeElement !== domNode`) covers the focused case while the port's echo covers the rest.

### 4.5 The edit template end to end

Walk: open a tiddler, click *edit*, type a title, type a body, open the tag picker, type `Uni`, press Enter, click a toolbar button, drop an image, press ctrl+Enter, confirm a discard. At width none today: edit opens (navigator, wired); the title `<input>` works; the body textarea **loses text on blur** (#23); the tag input works but **Enter never crosses** (gap #8) so the tag never adds by keyboard (click on the suggested tag works); the toolbar **never renders**; the drop **has no leg** (#5); ctrl+Enter crosses (modifier chord) and `$:/config/shortcuts/save-tiddler` fires only through the `$keyboard` wrapper in the edit template, not the global manager; the discard **asks through the confirm road and works**. Under the contract every step lands or refuses by name; under full/skinny/story every step runs stock.

### 4.6 Dropzone, import, drag and drop

`$dropzone` binds six listeners plus three body-capture listeners; `$droppable` four; `makeDraggable` two plus a drag image; `$browse` one. All read `dataTransfer`, `files`, `clientX/Y` and `setDragImage`, none of which crosses a thread, and WorkerDOM never carried them either **[reached: fetched]**. **Fix:** page-only binding of the drop targets with page-side cancellation; a single `import-offer` or `drop` event with the whole resolved payload (titles parsed from `text/vnd.tiddler` on the page by the same `importDataTransferTypes` table, or bounded bytes); `startActions`/`endActions` as `drag-start`/`drag-end` events; `lar-order-list` as the base path for list reorder. **Refusal:** generic drag between arbitrary widgets refuses (`page-controls.mem`), and drops over `data-lar-max-bytes` answer `input-too-long` beside the zone. **Width:** none; stock elsewhere. **Hosts:** Mudlet and MCP receive an `import` tool or a file path, never a drag.

### 4.7 Keyboard: the manager, `$keyboard`, `$eventcatcher`

`$tw.keyboardManager` exists in the third runtime (survey §5.1) but nothing binds the document leg; `$keyboard` matches on `keyCode` plus modifiers and exposes `event.key`/`event.code` as variables, which the relay blanks. Today plain Enter, Tab, Escape-without-modal, arrows and `((input-accept))` family never cross unless modified. **Fix:** declared keys per binding (`data-lar-keys` from the widget's own `parseKeyDescriptors`), real `key`/`code`/`keyCode`/`repeat` on the event, a document leg driven by a `shortcuts` key the engine publishes, and `isMac` from the surface's manifest rather than `$tw.browser` (gap #8's platform mapping). **`$eventcatcher`:** stays REFUSED at none with a visible refusal; a future declared-selector binding would carry `{selector matched, target dataset, type}` and lose pointer capture; **open ruling 9.4**. **Width:** none; stock elsewhere.

### 4.8 IME composition

The sink guards `compositionstart/end`, drops `input` while composing, relays once on `compositionend` and swallows the trailing duplicate `input` (`projection-sink.ts:226-258` **[reached: code]**). Two holes: Safari fires the committing Enter `keydown` *after* `compositionend` with `isComposing === false`, so a declared-Enter binding (search, tag picker) fires on the commit keystroke and submits a half-composed value; the field recommends `keyCode === 229` as the composition tell and a short deferral after `compositionend` **[reached: search, WebKit bug 165004, Square engineering, W3C uievents #202]**. And a frame landing mid-composition that *replaces* the node (morph by id usually keeps it; a template change that re-keys it does not) tears the composition. **Fix:** treat `keyCode 229` as composing on every platform; hold a declared-key act for one task after `compositionend`; `beforeNodeMorphed` returns `false` for a composing node regardless of revision. **Width:** none; at full/skinny the browser and TW5 handle it as today in stock TW5 (which has its own IME history **[unreached]**).

### 4.9 Undo

Undo lives in the browser's edit history for the node. A morph that keeps the node by id preserves it; a frame that replaces the textarea (the `#23` repaint today, or a re-keyed template) destroys it, and a relayed whole value re-applied by the engine never restores it. **Fix:** the page never writes a field's `value` from a frame while the field holds a local revision; a *take theirs* act replaces the value as one undoable edit. At full/skinny undo stays stock. Mudlet's `Geyser.TextEdit` carries Qt undo *(inferred)*; MCP has none.

### 4.10 Navigation, permalinks, Back, scroll

`story.js` binds `hashchange`, `tm-permalink`, `tm-permaview`, `tm-home`, `tm-browser-refresh` only in the browser; the island never sets `$:/info/url/*`, so `meta-startup-action.mem` reads an empty hash (survey #17). **Fix:** `lar:navigate` service with a route key; the page composes `#` from the order key and pushes history; Back posts a `route` act; the engine answers with a new order key. Scroll-to-navigated reads as a page transition keyed on `$:/HistoryList`'s tail. **Hosts:** SSR renders a permalink as a real `href`; Mudlet and MCP carry a `render` of a title and no history.

### 4.11 The surface switch (#13)

The gate flips, nothing re-emits, clicks still route to the old island. **Fix:** `projection:resend` on `session:surface-open` and on switch, with a new `mountEpoch`; acts carry the epoch; an act with an old epoch answers `stale-target` (never applies to the hidden wiki). **Width:** none at the DOM sink; at full/skinny a switch opens a port and takes a snapshot.

### 4.12 Where a width or host loses by design, said plainly

- **Width none, any host:** rich text selection operations beyond the carried pair, pointer capture, `$eventcatcher` generic capture, arbitrary drag, `tm-http-request`, synchronous layout reads. Each refuses by name.
- **Skinny/story:** an act whose handler touches text the glass never held (`$text` on a skinny tiddler, export, a `$list` over bodies) must ask; a verb that runs on the glass against a skinny replica without an ask reads as blur (`third-ways.md` §4.1).
- **Node-served browser, SSR face:** output-only until the page attaches a surface; every form posts as a `write` or an `act` over the holder; no hash.
- **QuickJS/Hermes shells:** the engine runs here; the host supplies the sink; a React Native view tree as a blocks projection carries `TextInput` with the platform's own event-count handshake (a single-author analysis of controlled `TextInput` describes native keeping a counter and refusing a stale write **[reached: search]**), which reads as the same sensed-revision rule in native clothes.
- **UE6 sidecar:** acts arrive as `blocks` affordance invokes with the player as actor; edits as whole-value writes from a UMG box; no DnD, no clipboard, no popups beyond a panel.
- **Mudlet:** results and affordances only; `echoLink`/label click callbacks and command-line aliases invoke by id *(Mudlet UI function page unreached this pass, DNS failure; `mudlet-capabilities.md` §4.2 and memory)*; `Geyser.TextEdit` edits as whole writes; no key-level relay, no IME concerns beyond Qt's own.
- **MCP/chat:** `tools/call` for acts, `resources` for keys, elicitation for the confirm road (form mode: flat schema, `accept`/`decline`/`cancel` **[reached: fetched, 2025-11-25 spec]**), `tools/list_changed` as the affordance set changing; Discord components invoke by `custom_id` under a 3 s acknowledge and a 15 min token **[reached: search]**, which bounds how long a parked act may wait on a sleeping actor there.

---

## 5. Conformance: interaction goldens

The evaluator-neutral suite (`evaluators-one-or-many.md` §5: `filter-cts.json`, per-camera render goldens with declared tolerance, mandatory degradation cases) gains a third family. Shape, following the same rules (oracle first, reviewed once, frozen world, `since`, `host-bound`, degradation as a section):

```
{
  "name": "interaction/edit/body-survives-blur",
  "world": "worlds/pono-small",
  "camera": {"root": "$:/core/ui/RootTemplate", "sink": "dom" | "blocks" | "text" | "label-html", "width": "none" | "skinny" | "full"},
  "script": [
    {"act": "navigate", "to": "Lesson 3"},
    {"act": "edit"},
    {"sense": {"control": "draft.text", "value": "three paragraphs", "localRev": 1}},
    {"act": "focus", "control": "draft.tags"},
    {"frame": "deliver-older", "rev": "before-sense"},
    {"sense": {"control": "draft.text", "value": "three paragraphs\nfour", "localRev": 2}},
    {"act": "save"}
  ],
  "expect": {
    "writes":   [{"title": "Lesson 3", "fields": {"text": "three paragraphs\nfour"}}],
    "messages": ["tm-edit-tiddler", "tm-save-tiddler"],
    "answers":  [{"act": "save", "status": "applied"}],
    "frame":    {"keys": {"Lesson 3": {"contains": "three paragraphs\nfour"}}, "membership": ["Lesson 3"]},
    "page":     {"draft.text": {"value": "three paragraphs\nfour", "undoDepth": ">=2", "focus": "draft.tags"}}
  },
  "tags": ["interaction", "edit", "HIGH-23"], "host-bound": true, "since": "tw5 ea94ca8"
}
```

Rules: the *script* speaks the contract's vocabulary (`act`, `sense`, `write`, `service-result`, `frame` delivery control) and never a DOM API, so a Lua harness, a Playwright harness and an MCP harness run the same file; *expected writes* compare as records after the echo lands; *messages* compare the `tm-*` the root widget saw; *answers* compare by act index; the *frame* compares through the camera golden's own normaliser; a surface that has no road for a step records `{"refused": "<reason>"}` and the suite checks the refusal reads beside the control (the words of `page-controls.mem#/refusals`).

**The minimal set, fourteen scripts, each with the gap it pins:**

1. `link/ordinary-modified-middle-external` (#1): ordinary click navigates and answers `applied`; ctrl/middle suppress navigation; external `href` never cancelled; no act for an unbound node.
2. `button/actions-with-modifier-and-popup`: `actions` run with `modifier`; a popup opens as wiki state and the page places it from the act's geometry.
3. `edit/body-survives-blur` (#23, above).
4. `edit/peer-write-into-open-editor` (ruling condition 4): a store write lands while the field holds `localRev`; the page keeps its text, shows the newer version beside it, `take-theirs` replaces as one undo step.
5. `edit/toolbar-wrap-selection-carried-pair`: `tm-edit-text-operation` with `{value, sel}`; answer carries `want`; page applies while rev matches; a stale rev refuses `stale-target`.
6. `toggle/checkbox-radio-select-multiselect` (#4): each act writes the right field and the next frame paints it; the focused select never snaps back.
7. `keys/search-enter-tagpicker-enter-global-shortcut` (#8): declared keys cross with `key`/`code`; an undeclared key never leaves the page; `$:/tags/KeyboardShortcut` fires from the document leg.
8. `ime/safari-enter-after-compositionend` (§4.8): a committing Enter with `keyCode 229` never submits; the value lands once.
9. `import/file-pick-and-drop-json` (#5): `import-offer` parks `$:/Import`; `tm-perform-import` lands the tiddlers; oversize refuses `input-too-long`.
10. `drop/droppable-actions-and-order-write`: a drop with modifier runs `actions`; `lar-order-list` writes the whole list; an absent id never deletes a member.
11. `confirm/delete-asks-then-applies`: the question parks, a second ask withdraws the first, `yes` re-dispatches, a changed subject answers nothing and says so.
12. `services/copy-download-print-refuse-by-name` (#2): clipboard and download answer `applied` on a surface that carries them; print refuses `page-action-unavailable` with the alert.
13. `switch/resend-and-epoch` (#13): switching surfaces paints the new mount's first snapshot; an act with the old epoch answers `stale-target` and touches nothing.
14. `actor/wake-on-act-and-recipe-refusal` (§3.4): an act on a sleeping actor parks, the actor wakes, the act answers; an act into a recipe wiki refuses `actor-not-spawned`.

Each script runs at width full (stock TW5 as the oracle, in Playwright), at width none over the DOM sink, and over the blocks sink (headless, vitest); Mudlet and MCP rows run the subset their manifest carries and publish refusals for the rest. **Two-way parity** for a DreamDOM member then reads as: the same expected writes and messages at every width where the script runs, and a named refusal wherever it does not.

---

## 6. Prior art for the UP leg, placed

| Field | What it settled | What the house takes | Mark |
|---|---|---|---|
| WorkerDOM | a mutation stream down; events proxied up with `preventDefault` declared at subscribe; `focus`, `activeElement`, `Selection`, `Range`, `selectionStart/End`, `getBoundingClientRect`, `checked` unsupported after seven years | declare at binding; never promise programmatic focus or selection from the VM | [reached: fetched, `web_compat_table.md`] |
| remote-dom | `remoteEvents` declared on the element class; no bubbling unless asked; host allowlist of events; `respondWith()` returns a value to the caller | the allowlist as the binding declaration; `respondWith` as the `want` field | [reached: fetched, core README] |
| Phoenix LiveView | the JS client stays the source of truth for a focused input; `phx-patch-focused` opts in; `phx-auto-recover` re-sends `phx-change` after reconnect; submit disables inputs and restores the last focused one; invalid number inputs send no change; `beforeUpdate` runs synchronously and cannot cancel | the focused-field rule, generalised to `localRev > sensedRevision`; form recovery as the attachment's sensed state on wake; the `inputmode="numeric"` rule | [reached: fetched, form-bindings.md, js-interop.md] |
| Hotwire/Turbo, idiomorph, htmx | morph by id keeps focus and caret; `ignoreActiveValue`, `restoreFocus`, `beforeNodeMorphed`; `hx-preserve` cannot preserve a text input's focus; Turbo needs `data-turbo-permanent` | the per-control veto in `beforeNodeMorphed`; never trust `hx-preserve`-style wholesale preservation | [reached: fetched (idiomorph README); reached: search (htmx docs); unreached (Turbo, prior pass)] |
| Blazor Server | `@onclick:preventDefault` as an attribute because the handler runs after SignalR; frequent events slow; `@bind:event="oninput"` | the same attribute law; `input` as sense, `change` as act | [reached: search] |
| React Native / Hermes | controlled `TextInput` guarded by a native event count; a stale write refused | a sensed revision in native clothes for a blocks sink on RN | [reached: search, single-author analysis] |
| Game netcode | inputs with sequence numbers over a reliable lane; state snapshots droppable and relevance-culled; the server acks the last processed input | reliable acts with ids and acks beside droppable senses; no replay (both sides replicas) | [reached: search] |
| Mudlet / GMCP | `sendGMCP` client→server with JSON payloads; clickable text and label callbacks by Lua function; OSC 8 links | affordance invoke by id over `Lar.Invoke`; results never the language | [reached: search (GMCP); unreached this pass (UI functions page, DNS failure); sibling `mudlet-capabilities.md`] |
| Discord components | `custom_id` round-trips on click; 3 s acknowledge, 15 min follow-up token | affordance ids; a parked act's budget on chat hosts | [reached: search] |
| MCP elicitation | `elicitation/create` with form or URL mode; flat schema; `accept`/`decline`/`cancel` | the confirm road and `lar-field` schemas map onto form mode; `cancel` = withdrawn question | [reached: fetched, 2025-11-25 spec] |
| IME / UI Events | Safari's Enter after `compositionend` with `isComposing false`; `keyCode 229`; deferred commit | §4.8 | [reached: search; UI Events spec page unreached in full] |
| ARIA across shadow roots | IDREFs and `activeElement` break at the boundary (`dreamdom.mem#/the-borrowed`) | refusal rows for `aria-activedescendant` patterns; light-DOM controls in `page-controls` | [unreached, prior meme] |

